//  slice 1 — the coordination-plan (plan) target serializes via CHECKED
// Expected propagation, NEVER cantFail. A plan serialization / assemblePlan
// legality failure fails closed with a stable diagnostic and leaves NO partial
// coordination-plan.json / backend-projection.json behind — on BOTH the
// from-source and the --from-spec paths.
//
// Before  the from-source coordination-plan target re-serialized with
// cantFail(coordinationPlanToText(...)), so any newly-added assemblePlan legality
// error would crash / emit a corrupt coordination plan instead of a clean diagnostic. This
// pins the error seam; the mixed-temporal legality refusal that will USE it is a
// separate PR ( item 2) and is intentionally NOT added here.
//
// BITING PROPERTY (re-review): the hidden --coordination-plan-fault-selftest seam
// folds the failure INTO the Expected the serializer returns (it does NOT
// short-circuit before it), so the driver's ordinary `if (!planTextE) return
// fail(...takeError())` is the code under test. The fault runs assert EXACTLY
// exit 4 (EXIT_IR): if that checked unwrap were replaced by
// cantFail(coordinationPlanToText(...)) — the exact  regression — the
// injected error would abort the process (exit != 4) and these runs FAIL. So a
// cantFail reintroduction on either path is detected here, not silently green.
//
// RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
//
// ---- non-vacuity: the coordination-plan target succeeds WITHOUT the fault seam ----------
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=coordination-plan %S/coordination_plan.neu -o %t/ok
// RUN: test -e %t/ok/coordination-plan.json
// RUN: test -e %t/ok/backend-projection.json
//
// ---- from-source: a forced coordination-plan serialization failure fails closed --------
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=coordination-plan --coordination-plan-fault-selftest %S/coordination_plan.neu -o %t/neg; [ $? -eq 4 ]
// RUN: test ! -e %t/neg/coordination-plan.json
// RUN: test ! -e %t/neg/backend-projection.json
// RUN: %FileCheck --check-prefix=SEAMFAULT %s < %t/neg/diagnostics.json
//
// ---- --from-spec: the same seam, the same fail-closed behavior ------------
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=capability-spec %S/coordination_plan.neu -o %t/spec
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=coordination-plan --from-spec %t/spec/capability-spec.json --coordination-plan-fault-selftest -o %t/negrt; [ $? -eq 4 ]
// RUN: test ! -e %t/negrt/coordination-plan.json
// RUN: test ! -e %t/negrt/backend-projection.json
// RUN: %FileCheck --check-prefix=SEAMFAULT %s < %t/negrt/diagnostics.json
//
// The diagnostics bundle records the failure with the stable code and ok:false
// (FileCheck matches in file order: the diagnostic message precedes the ok flag).
// SEAMFAULT: forced-coordination-plan-serialization-failure
// SEAMFAULT: "ok": false
